<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fisher's principle of equal investment in the sexes" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Under random mating and autosomal inheritance, selection drives parents to invest equally in sons and daughters, which gives a 1:1 sex ratio when the two cost the same." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "ESS allocation: N_m c_m = N_f c_f; with c_m = c_f the unbeatable primary sex ratio is 1:1" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: panmixia, autosomal control of the sex ratio, each offspring has one father and one mother, no local mate competition or sex-specific resource competition. Formal status: proved as an invasion (ESS) result (Shaw and Mohler 1953). Its own named exceptions (local mate competition, Hamilton 1967) are predicted deviations, not refutations." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Compare population sex-investment ratios (numbers times per-offspring cost) across species that meet the panmixia assumption, and test that experimentally perturbed sex ratios return toward equal investment." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "Ronald A. Fisher (1930) The Genetical Theory of Natural Selection" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/fisher-sex-ratio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1086/281794> .
}
